# hardthz course
version 1
title First steps
description Never touched a piano? Start here. Middle C, then its neighbours, the names of the white keys, the black ones, and your left hand: a little at a time, at your own pace.
instrument piano

unit Meet the keyboard

lesson Middle C
title White keys and black keys
text A piano's keys go from low on the left to high on the right. The black keys come in groups: two, then three, then two again, all the way along.
text Those groups are how you find your way. A C is always the white key just left of a group of two black keys.
title Middle C
text The C nearest the middle of the keyboard is middle C. hardthz marks it with a dot, and lights it now: press it with your right thumb.
text Plugged in a MIDI keyboard? hardthz plays from it. No keyboard? The computer's keys are the piano (the letter on each key plays it), or click the keys.
exercise
type notes
notes C4
show keys
count 3
pass 2

lesson Every C
title Octaves
text Twelve keys up from middle C, left of the next group of two black keys, is another C, higher. Twelve keys down, a lower one. From one C to the next is an octave.
text Play the C that lights up.
exercise
type notes
notes C3 C4 C5
show keys
count 6
pass 5

lesson C, D and E
title Your right hand
text Right thumb on middle C. Your fingers are numbered from the thumb: 1 the thumb, 2 the pointer, up to 5 the little finger.
text D is the white key between the two black ones, under finger 2. E is just right of them, under finger 3.
text Play them up, C D E, then back down.
exercise
type notes
notes C4 D4 E4 D4
show keys
order in_order
count 8
pass 7

lesson C, D, E in any order
text Now in any order: watch which key lights up.
exercise
type notes
notes C4 D4 E4
show keys
count 8
pass 7

lesson F, G, A and B
title By the three black keys
text F is the white key just left of the group of three black keys, under finger 4. Then G under finger 5.
text Above them, A and B, up to the next C. For those, move your hand: thumb on F, and fingers 2, 3, 4 on G, A, B.
exercise
type notes
notes F4 G4 A4 B4
show keys
count 8
pass 7

lesson Up to the next C
title Seven names, then again
text The white keys are named with seven letters, C D E F G A B, then C again: an octave higher, and the names go round.
text Play them all from middle C up to the next C, then back down.
exercise
type notes
notes C4 D4 E4 F4 G4 A4 B4 C5 B4 A4 G4 F4 E4 D4
show keys
order in_order
count 14
pass 12

lesson Any white key
text Any of them now, in any order.
exercise
type notes
notes C4 D4 E4 F4 G4 A4 B4 C5
show keys
count 12
pass 10

unit The names of the keys

lesson C, D and E by name
title A key by its name
text This time hardthz says the note's name, and lights its key too. Play it.
exercise
type notes
notes C4 D4 E4
show name
where yes
octave exact
count 8
pass 7

lesson C, D and E, no hints
text Now just the name: find it by the two black keys. A slip shows you where it was.
exercise
type notes
notes C4 D4 E4
show name
octave exact
count 8
pass 7

lesson F, G, A and B by name
text The same by the three black keys: F, G, A, B.
exercise
type notes
notes F4 G4 A4 B4
show name
where yes
octave exact
count 8
pass 7

lesson F, G, A and B, no hints
exercise
type notes
notes F4 G4 A4 B4
show name
octave exact
count 8
pass 7

lesson Seven names
text All seven white keys from middle C, by name.
exercise
type notes
notes C4 D4 E4 F4 G4 A4 B4
show name
octave exact
count 12
pass 10

lesson Any octave
title The same name, everywhere
text Every C is a C, every G a G, whichever octave. Play the name asked anywhere on the keyboard.
exercise
type notes
notes C3 D3 E3 F3 G3 A3 B3 C4 D4 E4 F4 G4 A4 B4 C5
show name
octave any
count 12
pass 10

unit The black keys

lesson Sharps
title Black keys
text A black key is named after a white one beside it. Just right of C is C sharp, written C#: the note a little higher than C.
text The same for each one: C#, D# between the two black keys, then F#, G#, A# among the three.
exercise
type notes
notes C#4 D#4 F#4 G#4 A#4
show keys
count 8
pass 7

lesson Sharps by name
text Now by name, the key lit too. C# is right of C, F# right of F.
exercise
type notes
notes C#4 D#4 F#4 G#4 A#4
show name
where yes
octave exact
count 8
pass 7

lesson Flats
title The same key, two names
text Seen from the other side, a black key is also the flat of the white key on its right: D flat, written Db, is the same key as C#.
text So the black keys are C# or Db, D# or Eb, F# or Gb, G# or Ab, A# or Bb. Music uses whichever suits the key it's in.
text Play the black keys as they light up.
exercise
type notes
notes C#4 D#4 F#4 G#4 A#4
show keys
count 8
pass 7

lesson All twelve
title Every key in an octave
text Seven white keys and five black ones: twelve, and then the next C. Play whichever lights up.
exercise
type notes
notes C4 C#4 D4 D#4 E4 F4 F#4 G4 G#4 A4 A#4 B4
show keys
count 12
pass 10

lesson Sharps, no hints
exercise
type notes
notes C#4 D#4 F#4 G#4 A#4
show name
octave exact
count 8
pass 7

unit Your left hand

lesson The C below middle C
title The low notes
text Your left hand plays the lower notes, left of middle C. Put its little finger, finger 5, on the C an octave below middle C.
exercise
type notes
notes C3
show keys
count 3
pass 2

lesson Five fingers, five keys
text Left hand, little finger on that C: fingers 5, 4, 3, 2, 1 rest on C, D, E, F, G. Play them up, then back down.
exercise
type notes
notes C3 D3 E3 F3 G3 F3 E3 D3
show keys
order in_order
count 8
pass 7

lesson Left hand, any order
exercise
type notes
notes C3 D3 E3 F3 G3
show keys
count 10
pass 8

lesson Left hand by name
text The left hand's five notes by name, their keys lit.
exercise
type notes
notes C3 D3 E3 F3 G3
show name
where yes
octave exact
count 8
pass 7

lesson Left hand, no hints
exercise
type notes
notes C3 D3 E3 F3 G3
show name
octave exact
count 8
pass 7

lesson Both hands
title Two hands, ten keys
text Both hands now: the left on C to G below middle C, the right on C to G from middle C. Play whichever key lights up, with the hand it's under.
exercise
type notes
notes C3 D3 E3 F3 G3 C4 D4 E4 F4 G4
show keys
count 12
pass 10
title What next
text You know your way round the keyboard, the white keys by name, the black ones, and both hands. The Reading course writes these same notes on the staff, the right hand's in the treble clef and the left hand's in the bass clef.
